# Pinned sources for `snapintosh build`. Override any value in the environment or in
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/snapintosh/pins.env.
#
# QEMU: upstream v11.1.0 plus the series in patches/qemu/ (24 patches, applied in order to the working tree of a shallow
# fetch of the tag's commit). The renderer sources (reims-vgpu, metal2vulkan) come as one checksummed release tarball (RENDERER_URL,
# RENDERER_SHA256 below); set REIMS_REPO or M2V_REPO only to build from a clone of your own.

# QEMU_REF is the commit of upstream tag v11.1.0 (gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu). The version string stays the plain tag
# because the patched tree is built without any commit on top (no `git describe` name), which keeps the binary reproducible.
# QEMU_PATCHED_HEAD is the last commit of the series (patches/qemu/0024), for reference.
# The patched tree equals that commit except for three em-dash characters replaced by " - " in two documentation files of patch 0002
# (AGENTS.md, docs/experiments/E0003...); no source file differs, so the binary is the same.
#
# Changelog of the series:
#   release-v0: TCG for the vmapple machine, Ambrosia machine layout and PAuth key copy to secondary CPUs, a persistent
#     content-keyed translation cache ("pack"), its compaction tool qemu-pcache-compact, IOFence matcher for known guest builds,
#     snapshot state for the avp-rtc, clock fix after a resume. Reference md5 on Debian 13: cf135e84fec1907c762beb52925fa288.
#   release-v1: the exit no longer msyncs the pack (the compaction tool fdatasyncs it). md5 455899b7d68dbf7ff41b8cec5a603956.
#   release-v2: a vCPU thread that wants the big QEMU lock spins for 50 us before it sleeps (P102_BQLSPIN=0 turns the spin off,
#     P102_BQLSPIN=N sets N microseconds). The pack format and the machine layout did not change, so a snapshot of release-v1
#     resumes with release-v2 and the other way round.
# Reference md5 of the release-v2 binary, `snapintosh build` from a clean tree on a minimal Debian 13 (renderer lib 97230a90a5d39d85f79df52358096de2):
# Debian 13: qemu-system-aarch64 c36556f3118e04fca90005ae0f0dfd68
# translation pack is new. Ubuntu 26.04 (gcc 15.2): qemu-system-aarch64 7bca48fbfa6f6d4954b5643890243d61, libreims_vgpu.a 3105d01f51d9b335d731c5b0ed1be662
# (the binary of each release is new, so each has a translation pack of its own; release-v0 on Ubuntu 26.04: 7a27d6f4a0181de261f5938440365958)
# `build` passes a fixed feature set to QEMU, so the md5 does not depend on which optional packages are installed.
# The unset-only default keeps QEMU_REPO="" meaning "no repository" (build then stops and says so).
QEMU_REPO=${QEMU_REPO-https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu.git}
QEMU_REF=${QEMU_REF:-84f07211cc5b4fc6a371559bf8a5de4fb068e648}
QEMU_PATCHED_HEAD=8df7ee62c81bc602b0eec0cd23c1fa11994a7094

# Renderer: reims-vgpu and metal2vulkan. Their upstream bases are no longer served, so the exact pinned trees (git archive of the two
# commits below, nothing edited or removed, gzip -n, sorted names, fixed owner and mtime) are one tarball of this project's release
# arm64-renderer-1. `build` downloads it once, refuses a file whose sha256 differs and never unpacks it then. Origin, base and our
# commits: docs/RENDERER.md. To rebuild the tarball: scripts/make-renderer-tarball.sh.
RENDERER_URL=${RENDERER_URL:-https://github.com/lucid-fabrics/osx-proxmox-next/releases/download/arm64-renderer-1/arm64-renderer-1.tar.gz}
RENDERER_SHA256=${RENDERER_SHA256:-c41ef7ac8f58d0b917e0fd22db8a1c50bd37f029832bb271e4c7f14215f0f357}
# metal2vulkan e0a40424: unordered framebuffer fetch without an interlock, no-copy buffers over dma-bufs without host-pointer import,
# and the switches M2V_NO_INTERLOCK and M2V_NO_HOSTPTR. On a GPU that has the extensions the preferred paths still run.
# reims-vgpu 81e0125b: counts dma-buf host-memory import, and a wake after a snapshot save resumes the device in place without losing the
# root FIFO and the stamp memory (a child FIFO's next barrier used to abort the save).
# reims-vgpu expects metal2vulkan as a sibling directory (its Cargo.toml patches the git dependency to ../metal2vulkan).
REIMS_REPO=${REIMS_REPO-}
REIMS_REF=${REIMS_REF:-81e0125b5594639caff4a3fc7e38446e00cb499b}
M2V_REPO=${M2V_REPO-}
M2V_REF=${M2V_REF:-e0a4042424a36d96822b7eb7ab54f6a3af5ad1e2}

# Snapshot state format. A snapshot resumes with any build that has the same value: the QEMU
# fork's migration stream (vmstate of the vmapple machine and devices, from QEMU_REF) plus the renderer's suspend blob
# (reims-vgpu guest/abi/suspend_blob.rs, magic RVGS version 1). Relinking a renderer fix that leaves both alone keeps the
# value. BUMP IT whenever QEMU_REF changes a vmstate section or machine layout, or the blob version changes: `build` then keeps
# the old binary for the snapshots that still need it and `resume` picks it. Wrongly unchanged means a resume that fails to load or
# misbehaves; wrongly bumped only costs a kept binary.
SNAPSHOT_STATE_FORMAT=${SNAPSHOT_STATE_FORMAT:-vmapple-18bbe3b54b-rvgs1}

# Ambrosia (boot firmware, replaces Apple's AVPBooter and iBoot). Upstream is public. Tag v0.1.3 plus our 3
# optional-key patches in patches/ambrosia (KeepAppleGfx, Chosen, Asmb; kept as
# commits, head 2fa868c2daa6). License GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, our patches follow it.
# Builds with rust 1.99.1 (its rust-toolchain.toml) and the aarch64-unknown-none target, one `make`.
AMBROSIA_REPO=${AMBROSIA_REPO:-https://github.com/steelbrain/ambrosia.git}
AMBROSIA_REF=${AMBROSIA_REF:-1b924d95f077b6e84f300f40fe1dbd1788772f69}
AMBROSIA_PATCHED_HEAD=2fa868c2daa62128f78d01728379e31da76c05e5
# Image the release was tested with. `build` reproduces it byte for byte with rust 1.99.1 and warns if not.
AMBROSIA_SHA256=${AMBROSIA_SHA256:-586f6c7be1622a1f80c52e3fc1ab210464eb2b8e272616334625d940d66f0a73}

# Guest policy keys the guest needs under Ambrosia: internal-use-only-unit
# lets the Data volume mount, lp-sip0=127 (0x7f) is the old csr-config=0x7f and is needed for speed. Not a
# SIP-on configuration. Written into config.plist, packed as config.cpio, loaded at 0x120000000.
AMBROSIA_BOOTARGS=${AMBROSIA_BOOTARGS:--v}
AMBROSIA_LP_SIP0=${AMBROSIA_LP_SIP0:-127}

# Mesa, only for hosts without a usable Vulkan GPU (lavapipe). Stock lavapipe 25.0.x lacks
# VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock, which the renderer requires. The tested Mesa is 26.3.0
# development (0a6fa60abb73) plus patches/mesa-lavapipe-immutable-samplers.patch.
MESA_REPO=${MESA_REPO:-https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.git}
MESA_REF=${MESA_REF:-0a6fa60abb737d26ac8a316a4aad7c9ddf64f9e4}

# Tested guest builds. `snapintosh fetch --build B` picks one; Apple's CDN serves the file, we never host it.
# 26A428 (27.0) is the build every measured number comes from and the only one the full stack has booted.
# 26B131 (27.2.1, released 2026-11-09) is the supported second path: the IOFence
# matcher has its row, Ambrosia upstream lists it as tested, but this stack has NOT booted it, and the quiet
# profile, harness boxes and apple-gfx guest side are unchecked there. Needs its own Mac install and golden.
IPSW_BUILDS="26A428 26B131"
IPSW_DEFAULT=${IPSW_DEFAULT:-26A428}
IPSW_26A428_VERSION=27.0
IPSW_26A428_URL=https://updates.cdn-apple.com/2026FallFCS/afcfc88e-bbe6-44bf-a5da-07c56eebc06c/UniversalMac_27.0_26A428_Restore.ipsw
IPSW_26A428_SHA256=2a5d3c695d501022b7fad9adaffcf2627bcb867d993fb5662dcd41bac99a2836
IPSW_26A428_SIZE=26626436228
IPSW_26B131_VERSION=27.2.1
IPSW_26B131_URL=https://updates.cdn-apple.com/2026FallFCS/c202a724-db7e-4d56-917b-110aa0226507/UniversalMac_27.2.1_26B131_Restore.ipsw
IPSW_26B131_SHA256=233e85a09887579d47d0b195e7db72be7f204261059c6946f719acf6b300814f
IPSW_26B131_SIZE=25595954706
# Index used to look a build up by id when a URL goes stale (third party, links go to Apple).
IPSW_INDEX=https://api.ipsw.me/v4/device/VirtualMac2,1?type=ipsw

# AVPBooter.vmapple2.bin is NOT a required input any more. Only the legacy path (FW=avp) uses it, and it must come
# from your own Mac (Apple file, never redistributed).
